; a full binary tree has exactly one more leaf than internal nodes: count e = nodes e + 1 (stated count e = s(nodes e)).
; count = leaves (Leaf->1, Node->cl+cr); nodes = internal (Leaf->0, Node->1+nl+nr). By tree induction: Leaf -> 1 = s(0); Node -> count l + count r = s(nodes l) + s(nodes r) [IHs] = s(s(nodes l + nodes r)) [right-succ] = s(nodes(Node l r)). The classic |leaves| = |internal|+1 identity for full binary trees -- a structural counting invariant.
